            <title>[LU-21076] llite: a stale OSC cat_size overwrites an MDT file size, breaking append, lseek and fallocate</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21076</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;cat_size is authoritative for the OSC layer only. ll_update_inode()&lt;br/&gt;
installs body-&amp;gt;mbo_size straight into i_size and never touches the&lt;br/&gt;
cl_attr, so i_size can legitimately be newer than cat_size. On a&lt;br/&gt;
PFL layout it stays that way for as long as a component is unlocked and its&lt;br/&gt;
LVB is stale.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both vvp_prep_size() and ll_merge_attr() then write that stale&lt;br/&gt;
cat_size over the newer size, and the callers that read i_size right&lt;br/&gt;
back suffer for it:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;an append takes its offset from it - vvp_io_write_start();&lt;br/&gt;
lseek() turns a too small size into -ENXIO -&lt;br/&gt;
vvp_io_lseek_start();&lt;br/&gt;
fallocate() sizes its request from it.&lt;br/&gt;
Fix&lt;br/&gt;
Track where i_size came from. LLIF_SIZE_FROM_MDT marks it as newer&lt;br/&gt;
than the OSC attributes, and neither vvp_prep_size() nor&lt;br/&gt;
ll_merge_attr() lowers it while the flag is set.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The flag is cleared where the OSC attributes become the newer ones:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;in cl_glimpse_lock(), where cl_lock_request() has either refreshed&lt;br/&gt;
the LVBs by a glimpse RPC or matched a lock over the whole file, in which&lt;br/&gt;
case cat_size is maintained locally;&lt;br/&gt;
in vvp_do_vmtruncate(), where this client has just set the size itself.&lt;br/&gt;
A remote truncate is therefore still able to shrink i_size - sanityn&lt;br/&gt;
test_16i.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ll_inode_size_lock() is deliberately not taken in ll_update_inode():&lt;br/&gt;
ll_lov_setstripe_ea_info() already holds it across&lt;br/&gt;
ll_intent_file_open() -&amp;gt; ll_prep_inode() -&amp;gt; ll_update_inode().&lt;/p&gt;</description>
